CENSUS OF IDEAS: THE FFMPEG-MUSIC STUDIOS AS AN INSTRUMENT LIBRARY

Final version, 2026-10-08. All six studios (100–600) are finished, and each has
a JOURNAL and a HANDOFF. 000 is the setup studio. Sources read: GENRE, NOTEBOOK
(whole discoveries log), research/01-ideas, every journal and handoff, every pieces/*.sh
(headers in full; commands for every piece that introduced a mechanism), every
sketches/*.sh|*.txt, the helper-tool headers, instruments/diatonic-live.sh,
perform.py and research/04-instrument-library. Nothing in studios/ was
modified. The first snapshot of this census covered 000–600 at mid-session. This
version adds what appeared afterwards (200: 204–206; 300: 304–306; 400: 406–409;
500: 504–509; 600: 604–606, plus their sketches and NOTEBOOK entries). It keeps
the original IDs, so the proposal's references still resolve, and appends new
IDs.

The question. Can the strongest ideas be pulled out of their pieces as
instruments: reusable building blocks with an interface that a composer, or a
live performer, could pick up?

Conventions in this document
- Type is one of: generator (makes sound or an image from nothing or from data),
  processor (transforms a stream), score (decides what/when; outputs numbers,
  masks or images that something else voices), tuning-system (a geometry that
  fixes pitch and time together), mix-tool (gain, stereo, dynamics, routing).
  Shared plumbing that is not an instrument is listed at the end.
- Live asks whether the parameters that matter could change during playback. yes
  = they are options marked T at the option level (ffmpeg -h filter=X, checked
  on this machine's ffmpeg 9.0.1), so they can be turned in real time from the
  stdin console or scheduled with asendcmd. knob = not directly, but the stage
  is an aeval that can read a live control channel (the knob-register pattern,
  proven in instruments/diatonic-live.sh). no = baked in at graph build time
  (aevalsrc/aeval/geq expressions, spectrumsynth, minterpolate, uspp, aecho,
  asetrate, aresample, axcorrelate, perspective, life, showwaves, demuxer
  -ar/-sample_rate all have no runtime options).
- Coupling: low = it already lives as a shell function or a template; med = it
  has to be lifted out of a piece's shared state (e.g. st/ld slots, global
  clocks); high = it only makes sense inside that piece's geometry.
- "(inferred)" marks anything I worked out from the code rather than found
  stated in the files. "(verified)" marks something I ran myself for this
  census.

LIVE CONTROL: WHAT I CHECKED

- aeval exprs, geq lum and uspp qp all reject runtime commands ("Function not
  implemented") even though ffmpeg -filters lists aeval, geq and uspp with T at
  the filter level (verified). The filter-level flag is unreliable in the other
  direction too: sidechaincompress/acompressor show .. but their options are T.
  Always check at the option level.
- Runtime options that matter for these instruments: afir dry/wet/ir (selects
  among up to 32 IR inputs), anlms/arls mu and out_mode, lagfun decay, gblur
  sigma, rotate angle, tmix weights, blend all_expr, crop x/y, scale w/h,
  zoneplate k-params, afreqshift/aphaseshift shift, volume, amix weights, adelay
  delays, the biquads (lowpass/highpass/bandpass/equalizer), dynaudnorm,
  acrusher, alimiter, sidechaincompress, atempo tempo, afade; and, for the newer
  pieces, surround (every in/out level, focus, angle, smooth), silenceremove
  (start/stop thresholds and modes) and drawtext (text, x, y, fontsize,
  fontcolor).
- The knob pattern (verified): aevalsrc=1,volume@knob=1:eval=frame makes a DC
  stream whose value can be changed by a command; amerge it beside an audio
  stream and aeval reads it as val(1). A volume 0.25 command dropped the product
  from 0 dB to −12 dB, with about one audio frame of latency. So any instrument
  whose maths sits in an aeval (not aevalsrc) can take live parameters. Any
  aevalsrc generator can be rewritten as an aeval over a clock or knob stream (t
  and n exist in aeval) (inferred; instruments/diatonic-live.sh does exactly
  this for 002).
- Image instruments (geq scores) cannot read audio, so their live handles are
  downstream video filters: blend expression, crop scroll, gblur, lagfun,
  rotate, tmix, lut/curves, and drawtext text (inferred).
- Commands only arrive through asendcmd/sendcmd (a timeline written into the
  command). This build has no zmq/azmq filters (verified absent), so real-time
  external control would need an FFmpeg built with libzmq (inferred from
  FFmpeg's docs, not tested). Correction (Claude, 2026-10-08): not needed —
  ffmpeg's interactive stdin console ('c' + target -1 command arg) accepts
  commands from a pipe in real time. Verified; see instruments/diatonic-live.sh
  and perform.py. Re-verified for this final version: piping c then volume@k -1
  volume 0.25 into a running ffmpeg (paced by arealtime) moved the measured peak
  from −18.1 dB to −30.1 dB mid-stream, and the reply was ret:0. perform.py
  drives this console from the keyboard, plays to -f audiotoolbox -, and with
  --record writes the knob moves back out as asendcmd in a new single-command
  piece. A performance can become a score.
- Practical consequence: "live" now means real time, not only timeline. The
  limit is still which options are runtime. Any expression-level change needs a
  knob register.

