2. PER-IDEA ENTRIES

GENERATORS

G1 SHEPARD STAIR

- From: 000/001-endless-stair (drone).
- Sound: an endlessly rising glissando of nine octave-spaced sines under a fixed
  spectral bell.
- Mechanism: aevalsrc, partial i at octave mod(i+t/20,9), gaussian weight
  exp(-(x-4.5)^2/3), phase as the closed-form integral of an exponential sweep
  (sin(1154.16*PI*2^x)) so there are no clicks; doubled through afreqshift=0.37
  for the other ear (M1).
- Instrument: in: nothing. Out: mono/stereo audio. Params: rate (octaves per s;
  1/20 used), partial count (9), bell centre/width, base frequency. 000's
  HANDOFF suggests a rising chord-tone stack instead of octaves; untried. 400's
  handoff proposes the same idea for read rates ("a Risset-style continuous
  zoom" of P4); untried.
- Coupling: low. Live: knob.

G2 HASH-GRAIN FM CLOUD

- From: 000/001 (cloud).
- Sound: sparse-to-swarming FM bell grains picked from a harmonic series.
- Mechanism: per-step hash noise mod(sin(k*12.9898)*43758.5453,1) picks pitch
  and gates the grain (lt(hash, density)); FM bell with exponential index decay.
- Instrument: in: none. Out: audio. Params: grain rate (16/s, 2/s layers),
  density 0.1→0.85, harmonic set, FM ratio (√2, e). Coupling: low. Live: knob
  (density is the obvious fader).
- Note (500, NOTEBOOK): random(i) keeps its seed in register i. Any st(i,…)
  every sample turns the "noise" into DC, as happened in 503's snare. Give
  random its own slot.

G3 EXPRESSION VOICES (SINE-DROP KICK, HASH HAT, FM PLUCK)

- From: 000/002, 300/302 (kick), 500/502 (teacher song); realised as a live
  instrument in instruments/diatonic-live.sh (pad + Barbieri arp + bass + kick,
  with knobs degree / mode / density / tone).
- Sound: the basic synth-drum and plucked-synth vocabulary, written as
