G16 MODAL ROOM, N-DIMENSIONAL, WITH A WALKING LISTENER

- From: 500/501, 502, 503, 505-tesseract, 507.
- Sound: a room tuned to a chord: modes = harmonic series on each axis, cross
  modes = shimmer. 505 is a 4-D room (D F# A C# = Dmaj7) whose six listening
  places voice the chord differently (corner = low Dmaj7, centre = octave up,
  halfway along D = F#m, halfway along A and C# = D/F#).
- Mechanism: nested while() modal sum in aevalsrc, f = sqrt(Σ(lᵢ·fᵢ)²),
